{
  "$comment": "What each annotation reader answers, as every implementation must answer it: TypeScript (@semiont/core, re-exported by @semiont/sdk), Rust (semiont::annotations) and Python (semiont.annotations) each run every case and fail on a difference. An `annotation` is as the wire carries it. `reads` names each reader that applies to it, by the name every SDK spells in its own convention (`bodySource` is getBodySource, body_source), and what it answers: `null` for nothing. A reader of a part is given that part: bodySource and isBodyResolved the body, targetSource and targetSelector the target, exactText and textQuoteSelector the target's selector. Every case states every reader, but textQuoteSelector where the target has no selector to give it. Add a case here before changing an implementation.",
  "readers": [
    "bodySource",
    "isBodyResolved",
    "targetSource",
    "targetSelector",
    "isHighlight",
    "isReference",
    "isAssessment",
    "isComment",
    "isTag",
    "commentText",
    "isStubReference",
    "isResolvedReference",
    "exactText",
    "annotationExactText",
    "textQuoteSelector",
    "entityTypes",
    "tagCategory",
    "tagSchemaId"
  ],
  "cases": [
